51
00:05:47.766 --> 00:05:56.332
Judge number three raised her eyebrows. "You aren't the best dancers we've seen today, but you

52
00:05:56.333 --> 00:06:02.490
certainly solved your problem in an original way." Mr. D. leaned into the mic and

53
00:06:02.491 --> 00:06:09.505
pointed to Javier. "You have to credit this guy for that. He really kept this

54
00:06:09.506 --> 00:06:13.330
crew together." "I think we know how this is going to end, panel, but are you

55
00:06:13.331 --> 00:06:20.219
ready to vote?" asked Judge number one. The judges pressed their buzzers. B-Frank was moving

56
00:06:20.220 --> 00:06:23.892
on to the next round of auditions! They were being held next month in New York

57
00:06:23.893 --> 00:06:27.968
City! "Alana, make sure you get these guys on camera!" Judge number one called to

58
00:06:27.969 --> 00:06:32.718
the show host who'd been interviewing contestants. "America will want to hear their story." "We're going

59
00:06:32.719 --> 00:06:41.479
to be on TV! We're going to New York!" All the guys were jumping up

60
00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:48.019
and down—including Mr. D. *** Later that afternoon, after they'd finished their interview, the crew

61
00:06:48.020 --> 00:06:54.052
went back to Holding Room C to pick up their things. Malcolm and Marty came over

62
00:06:54.053 --> 00:06:58.526
to offer some half-hearted congratulations. "You guys were pretty good," Malcolm said. "Yeah, pretty good,"

63
